### Chairs' Discussion & Best Path Next-Hop Selection Enhancements
* **Presenters:** Susan Hares, Olivier de Saint Martin
* **Drafts:** `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-nh-selection`, `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-selection-criteria`
* **Slides:** [Chairs's Discussion on Next-hop Selection](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-idr-sessa-1-5-1-chairss-discussion-on-next-hop-selection-01), [BGP Best Path Next-hop Selection Enhancements](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-idr-sessa-1-5-2-bgp-best-path-next-hop-selection-enhancements-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Susan Hares introduced a roadmap addressing next-hop resolution and path selection modifications across various IDR drafts.
  * Olivier de Saint Martin presented `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-nh-selection`. The draft formalizes BGP next-hop resolution by defining Path Resolution Tuples (Resolution Key + optional Resolution Context) and Resolution Constraints to prevent traffic drops or suboptimal path selection in tunnel-based architectures (e.g., MPLS, SRv6 Flex-Algo).
  * Authors of `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-nh-selection` plan to collaborate and merge concepts with `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-selection-criteria`.
  * Kalyan Kalvagadda noted similarities to BGP CAR/CT resolution schemes and stressed the need for standardized metric comparison across different tunnel types.
  * Robert Raszuk noted in the chat that this work pertains to selecting the underlying path/tunnel to reach a next hop rather than traditional next-hop resolution itself.

