### Strict Only to Customer (OTC) Verification on Route Server Sessions
* **Presenter:** Bryton Herdes
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-idr-otc-rs-verification`
* **Slides:** [Strict Only to Customer (OTC) Verification on Route Server Sessions](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-idr-sessa-1-7-strict-only-to-customer-otc-verification-on-route-server-sessions-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Bryton Herdes presented `draft-ietf-idr-otc-rs-verification`, which updates RFC 9234 OTC ingress checks for route server clients.
  * The draft adds a check requiring a route server client to verify whether an OTC attribute received on a route server session matches the route server's remote AS. If an OTC is present and does not match the route server AS, the route is rejected, preventing route leaks through route servers that have not implemented RFC 9234.
  * OpenBGPD and FRRouting (FRR) have already implemented this check (requiring minimal 1–2 line code modifications).
  * Serge Maskit and Bryton Herdes supported fast-tracking the document. Sriram Parameswaran clarified that the check applies to the remote AS of the peering session and volunteered to review the draft.

